;; world/rooms/glasswood/x0y4.room
(room
  region: glasswood
  at: (0 4)
  title: "Scree Foot"
  intent: "the foot of the scree, where a pale green stone is set in the rock: a door you cannot open yet"
  bed: (wind 0.4 water 0.2 hum 0.3 drone 0.5)
  grid:
  ("%%%%%%%%%%          #####"
   "%%%%%%%%%%    |     #####"
   "%%%%%%%%%%    |     #####"
   "%%%%%%%%%%    |     #####"
   "%%%%%%%%%%    |     #####"
   "              |  ########"
   "              |  #    ###"
   "              |  o    ###"
   "#################%  %####"
   "#################%  %####"
   "#################%  %####")
  things: ((ring-stone at: (17 7) overtone: 3))
  decor: auto)
;; Under the scree's shoulder (its rough face, column 9, is the climb back
;; up to the Scree). The pale green stone (17,7), keyed to H3, is the door
;; of a small chamber over the Cave Mouth's shaft (columns 18-19): carrying
;; H2 you pass within four tiles and it shivers off-key; coming up the
;; shaft carrying H3 it rings from inside and opens, and stays open. Calls
;; you from the caves (D45). West under the scree to the Icicle Walk.
